    "paragraph": "A Decision Tree Regressor evaluated on 14.2 million street-level crime records in London predicts monthly crime counts across 16,110 Lower Layer Super Output Areas with a Mean Absolute Error of 0.242. GITSR introduces a graph interaction transformer-based scene representation framework for multi-vehicle collaborative decision-making in mixed traffic environments containing connected automated vehicles and human-driven vehicles. Using a balanced panel of 16 South Korean metropolitan cities and provinces from 2012 to 2023, a Spatial Durbin Model evaluated how migrant labor relates to regional Gross Regional Domestic Product per capita across different skill levels and industrial structures.",
